# Patch series through 0032 (resident header resolver, one environment
# registry, generated exports) — the pin qed64 serves as runtime
# wasm64-5dcdda005a7c5ae0. Bumped 2026-09-07 from 852d1b9 for the resident
# transport port (the pump transport the game used was removed upstream).
# A stage1 rebuild from a new pin REQUIRES rebaking every game snapshot
# (init/testgame/nng4) against it: wasm/build-from-source.sh does all lanes.
# The `patch` line is that series' last patch and the kernel commit that
# completed it, machine-read: the qed64 package's workers state the oldest
# kernel patch they drive (embedding/closure.json runtime.minKernelPatch), and
# scripts/stage-workers.sh (every build and deploy) and the from-source
# preflight refuse workers that need a newer kernel than this one. The
# preflight also checks the number against the kernel: that commit must be
# an ancestor of (or equal to) the pinned SHA above — a pin moved back past
# its patch fails there, not in a browser. Bump both with the pin (the
# kernel's commit subjects do not reliably carry the number: 0031, 0033 and
# 0034 do not).
